            "verdict": "benign",
            "normalizedStatus": "clean",
            "analysis": "Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: kubernetes\nVersion: 1.0.6\n\nThe skill bundle is a comprehensive and well-documented platform engineering suite for Kubernetes and OpenShift management. It features a sophisticated multi-agent coordination system with explicit roles, persistent state tracking (via WORKING.md and SESSION.md), and mandatory human-in-the-loop guardrails for all destructive or production-altering actions (defined in AGENTS.md and QUICKREF.md). While some scripts contain potential shell injection vulnerabilities due to the use of 'eval' for constructing curl commands (e.g., in metric-query.sh and log-search.sh), these appear to be unintentional coding flaws rather than evidence of malice. The bundle includes a robust SECURITY.md policy and utility scripts for binary verification, indicating a strong focus on operational safety.",
            "source": "palm",
